From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:08:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: build the vendor overlay on 6.18

The vendor overlay does not build and link against the 6.18 driver.
It calls a routine of the switch PHY driver, which this target does
not build. It also reads a net_device pointer that the 6.18 driver
removed from the GDM device.

A weak stub resolves the call, so the real routine wins if that
driver is built. The GDM device has the pointer again, set at
allocation. The overlay reads it in many places, and the overlay
files must stay equal to the vendor files.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c  |    1 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h  |    1 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dp_api.c |    7 ++++++-
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dp_api.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dp_api.c
@@ -61,7 +61,12 @@ extern int (*dynamic_ifc_pingpong_hook)(
 extern spinlock_t ppe_lock, flow_offload_lock;
 extern unchar ethmac_addr[6];
 
-extern void EphyMonitor(void);
+/* EphyMonitor lives in the EPHY/switch PHY driver, which is out of scope
+ * for AN7581 PON; provide a weak no-op so the link resolves and the real
+ * implementation wins if that driver is ever built in.
+ */
+void __weak EphyMonitor(void);
+void __weak EphyMonitor(void) { }
 extern int g_pon_serdes_eth;
 
 /* airoha pon onu type
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4073,6 +4073,7 @@ static int airoha_alloc_gdm_device(struc
 
 	netdev->dev.of_node = of_node_get(np);
 	dev = netdev_priv(netdev);
+	dev->dev = netdev;
 	u64_stats_init(&dev->stats.syncp);
 	dev->port = port;
 	dev->eth = eth;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -665,6 +665,7 @@ struct airoha_gdm_dev {
 	struct airoha_qdma __rcu *qdma;
 	struct airoha_gdm_port *port;
 	struct airoha_eth *eth;
+	struct net_device *dev;
 
 	DECLARE_BITMAP(qos_sq_bmap, AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS);
 	/* qos stats counters */
